<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified">
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
REQUEST schema for couponPost (Customer360). This XML is carried in the form field 'XmlInput'.
Audited 2026-10-12 against the loyalty-app service generation.

couponPost CONSUMES a coupon: on success (RESPONSE_CODE S104) the coupon is marked as scanned,
and when CUSTOMER_ID is supplied the coupon is linked to that customer. Use couponAuthentication
for a read-only check.

Reading rules of the service:
  - Only the REQUEST child of the root is inspected; the root element name itself is not checked.
  - REQ_TRANSACTION_DETAILS and REQ_COUPON_DETAILS may appear in either order, as may their children.
  - Element names are case-sensitive.
  - When the tenant has a coupon prefix configured and enabled, a leading prefix is stripped
    from REQ_COUPON_CODE before lookup; the response still echoes the code as sent.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>
  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Top-level wrapper for the couponPost request envelope.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="REQUEST">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Request payload used to post (redeem/record) a coupon against a transaction.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:all>
              <xs:element name="REQ_TRANSACTION_DETAILS" minOccurs="0">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Transaction context in which the coupon is being posted. Optional: when REQ_STORE_ID is not supplied the service falls back to a default store of the tenant.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                  <xs:all>
                    <xs:element name="REQ_STORE_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The store at which the coupon is redeemed, matched exactly as sent (no zero-padding is applied). An unknown store returns RESPONSE_CODE E127. When omitted or empty, a default store of the tenant is used. The coupon's promotion must be assigned to this store (otherwise E113).</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="REQUEST_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The date and time of this request. Accepted but not interpreted by the service (any text is tolerated); ISO 8601 is recommended, e.g. 2026-10-12T15:00:00Z. The scan time recorded on the coupon is the server clock.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Optional customer identifier of the person redeeming the coupon. When supplied it must identify an existing customer, otherwise the service returns RESPONSE_CODE E855 and nothing is posted. On success the coupon is linked to this customer.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                  </xs:all>
                </xs:complexType>
              </xs:element>
              <xs:element name="REQ_COUPON_DETAILS">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Identifies the coupon being posted.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                  <xs:all>
                    <xs:element name="REQ_COUPON_CODE" type="xs:string">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The coupon code being posted (as scanned or keyed at the POS). Missing or empty returns RESPONSE_CODE E116.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="REQ_COUPON_TYPE">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Coupon issuance model. REQUIRED in practice: it must equal the type of the promotion the coupon belongs to, otherwise the service returns RESPONSE_CODE E842. There is NO server-side default (the earlier published default of SERIALIZE is not applied; a missing or empty value yields E842). NOTE: the non-serialized value is NONSERIALIZE with no hyphen; the previously published value NON-SERIALIZE never matches and always yields E842.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:simpleType>
                        <xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
                          <xs:enumeration value="SERIALIZE">
                            <xs:annotation>
                              <xs:documentation>Serialized coupons allow merchandisers to create large numbers of coupons with usage limits and randomly generated coupon codes in order to closely target and monitor coupon use.</xs:documentation>
                            </xs:annotation>
                          </xs:enumeration>
                          <xs:enumeration value="NONSERIALIZE">
                            <xs:annotation>
                              <xs:documentation>Non-serialized coupons: one shared code for the whole promotion.</xs:documentation>
                            </xs:annotation>
                          </xs:enumeration>
                        </xs:restriction>
                      </xs:simpleType>
                    </xs:element>
                  </xs:all>
                </xs:complexType>
              </xs:element>
            </xs:all>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
